# Safety (Always On)

Full policy: `@SAFETY.md`. Enforce these in every Cursor session:

## Tiers

| Tier | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| Allowed | Reads, search, `git status` / `log` / `diff` — proceed |
| Guarded | Working-dir writes, read-only shell — proceed; log intent |
| Restricted | Delete, mutating shell, `git push`, API writes — **stop and get approval** |

## Before any mutating tool

1. Classify read-only vs mutating.
2. Run destruction checks from `@SAFETY.md` (data loss, scope blast, irreversible git, secrets, prod).
3. If destructive → Restricted regardless of default tier.
4. Active safety flags in `logs/safety-flags.jsonl` → revoke Guarded until cleared.

## Deny by default

- No editing `.env`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, or credential files without explicit approval.
- No `rm -rf`, force push to main, or schema drops without explicit approval.
- Never bypass pre-commit hooks unless user explicitly requests.
